DEPENDS ON WWW::Crawl4AI ticket (Expose response_headers on crawl Result).

Net::Async::Crawl4AI needs NO production code change -- crawl_once funnels through WWW::Crawl4AI::Client::parse_crawl_response -> _normalize_page, and builds the Result via WWW::Crawl4AI::Result->from_attempt. So once WWW exposes response_headers, the async path inherits it.

This ticket = lock that inheritance with a regression test, because Goldmine uses the ASYNC client at runtime (na_crawl4ai_client). If a future refactor gives NET its own page-builder, the header exposure must not silently regress.

TEST
Mock/stub the HTTP layer to return a crawl JSON payload containing response_headers => { Link => q(<...>; rel="api-catalog"), q(Content-Type) => q(text/html) }. Run crawl(...)->get. Assert $result->response_headers->{link} present AND lowercased. One test, async harness already exists in t/.

Bump vendored WWW tarball dependency only after the WWW release.
